### IntelliJ HTTP Client: supply username/password in http-client.private.env.json (ignored by Git).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Must return 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/data

### Login: stores the access token in the HTTP Client's memory
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"{{username}}","password":"{{password}}"}

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Create a note (201); HTML must be escaped in the response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/data
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"<script>alert(1)</script>","content":"My private note"}

### Read only the current user's notes (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/data?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### SQL injection must return 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"' OR '1'='1' --","password":"incorrect-password"}

### Invalid JWT must return 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/data
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token
